From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@loudthinking.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur-anduril-bluechip: Drop rising-edge
 lid wakeup action

glymur-anduril-bluechip.dts inherits switch-lid (TLMM GPIO 92, active low)
with wakeup-event-action = <EV_ACT_DEASSERTED> from glymur-crd.dtsi. Armed
for the rising edge only, the lid IRQ fires and immediately wakes the
laptop on CX collapse exit when suspending with the lid open, matching the
same Glymur bug fixed on the Surface Laptop 8 and ASUS Zenbook A16.

Delete wakeup-event-action from switch-lid so opening a closed lid still
wakes the laptop while open-lid suspend stays asleep in CXSD/AOSD/DDR.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-anduril-bluechip.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-anduril-bluechip.dts	2026-11-27 15:22:55.799255915 +0100
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-anduril-bluechip.dts	2026-11-27 15:22:55.807406967 +0100
@@ -21,6 +21,12 @@
 	model = "Anduril BlueChip";
 	compatible = "anduril,bluechip", "qcom,glymur";
 
+	gpio-keys {
+		switch-lid {
+			/delete-property/ wakeup-event-action;
+		};
+	};
+
 	sound {
 		/*
 		 * Only the left woofer and tweeter answer on this board. The
